name: Scope membership survives staging changes, legacy history and explicit finite planning
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
require-env: KUZUSHI_LEGACY_NATIVE_BIN
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/git-config
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 MEMBERSHIP UNBOUND | legacy-source-visible
expect: Membership unbound; rebuild required
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME legacy-plan
ask: Does the legacy scope retain its historical approval while clearly requiring a new inventory before new work?
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | fresh-bound-inventory
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME bound
keys: a End Enter
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | accepted-two-files
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME stage-file
keys: a End Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Action stopped | staged-membership-refused
expect: membership changed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME staged-plan
ask: Does changed tracked membership refuse acceptance and planning even though SHA and source bytes are unchanged, with old history intact?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 30 Boundary: . | returned-from-refusal
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | new-tracked-file-included
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME updated
keys: f
require-live-snap: 30 later.rs | complete-membership
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 30 Boundary: . | returned-from-files
resize: 160x48
live-snap: bound-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: bound-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: bound-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: bound-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 r reload | bound-40x12
expect: Esc back
keys: NPage
live-snap: bound-paged-40x12
ask: Are actual membership, source limitations and reload/navigation controls understandable across sizes, with useful narrow paging?
resize: 120x36
keys: a End Enter
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | accepted-new-membership
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME prepare
ask: Does the new acceptance produce only three fixed unapproved jobs with one worker, while keeping legacy records and zero spending?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/git-config
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | recovered-new-membership
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_membership.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME restarted
ask: Does no-color restart recover the accepted three-file membership and preserve the old readable scope without starting jobs?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
